lisa-design:
- Chart choice is Go (internal/release ComponentTag + PickChart, `release chart`): the component is what precedes the first "-v" followed by a valid version; it matches a chart directory first, then a Chart.yaml name, because the product repo has charts/ccf-app whose Chart.yaml name is ccf (release-please's helm component may be either). A plain vX.Y.Z tag is allowed only when the repo has exactly one chart.
- Charts are packaged with --version <tag version>, not Chart.yaml's version: a cut-prerelease rc is tagged on main, whose Chart.yaml still has the previous version until the release PR merges. So no "Chart.yaml version == tag" check. Charts get no latest.
- release-helm.yml logs in with `helm registry login --password-stdin` (token never on argv); registry is an input defaulting to oci://ghcr.io/compliance-framework/helm-charts (the mocks push there too, under mock-* names).
- release-action.yml moves v<major> only for FINAL tags (an rc must not reach @v0 users), via the REST refs API with GITHUB_TOKEN (contents: write): PATCH force when the tag exists, POST when it's 404, fail on anything else. major comes from `release release-tags` (new major= output). No image is published: agent-action runs `image: Dockerfile`.
